cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use FaunaLapse, please cite it with the metadata below. Source code and documentation at https://github.com/valentinitnelav/fauna-lapse"
title: "FaunaLapse: a smartphone application for scheduled time-lapse monitoring of insects and other animals"
abstract: >-
  FaunaLapse is an offline Android application that turns old or low-cost phones
  into time-lapse cameras watching one spot, for example pollinators visiting a
  flower. It records short photo bursts or video clips on a daily schedule with the
  screen off, keeps only a user-chosen square region of interest, and closes the
  camera between bursts to save energy and limit heat, so a phone can run for longer.
  Every photo and video is logged together with field metadata. Source code and
  documentation at https://github.com/valentinitnelav/fauna-lapse
type: software
license: AGPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/valentinitnelav/fauna-lapse"
version: "0.1.0-beta.1"
date-released: "2026-10-12"
